sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant GW as External Gateway<br/>(Kuadrant/Authorino)
    participant API as API Server<br/>8000/TCP HTTP/HTTPS
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>TCP
    participant S3 as S3 Storage<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant Redis as Redis/Valkey<br/>TCP
    participant Proc as Processor<br/>(StatefulSet)
    participant Infer as llm-d Inference GW<br/>HTTP/HTTPS
    participant GC as Garbage Collector
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over Client,Infer: Flow 1: Batch Job Submission
    Client->>GW: POST /v1/files (upload JSONL)<br/>Auth: Bearer Token
    GW->>API: Forward request<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>S3: Upload input file<br/>AWS credentials
    S3-->>API: File stored
    API->>PG: Insert file record (tenant_id)<br/>Connection URL auth
    PG-->>API: File ID
    API-->>GW: 200 File object
    GW-->>Client: File upload response

    Client->>GW: POST /v1/batches<br/>input_file_id, model, endpoint
    GW->>API: Forward request<br/>X-MaaS-Username: tenant-id
    API->>PG: Insert batch job (tenant_id)<br/>Connection URL auth
    PG-->>API: Batch ID
    API->>Redis: Enqueue job to priority queue<br/>Connection URL auth
    Redis-->>API: Queued
    API-->>GW: 200 Batch object (status: validating)
    GW-->>Client: Batch created

    Note over Proc,Infer: Flow 2: Batch Job Processing
    Proc->>Redis: BLPOP from priority queue
    Redis-->>Proc: Batch job
    Proc->>PG: Update status → in_progress
    Proc->>S3: Download input JSONL
    S3-->>Proc: Input file contents

    loop For each inference request (AIMD-controlled concurrency)
        Proc->>Infer: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>Optional TLS 1.2+ / mTLS
        Infer-->>Proc: Inference result
    end

    Proc->>S3: Upload output JSONL
    S3-->>Proc: Output stored
    Proc->>PG: Update status → completed<br/>Set output_file_id

    Note over GC,K8s: Flow 3: Garbage Collection & Reconciliation
    GC->>PG: Query expired jobs/files
    PG-->>GC: Expired items
    GC->>S3: Delete expired files
    GC->>PG: Delete expired records
    GC->>K8s: Watch processor pods<br/>ServiceAccount token
    K8s-->>GC: Pod status events
    Note over GC: Detect crashed processors
    GC->>Redis: Re-enqueue orphaned jobs
